{
  "function": "content_sha256(body) -> str",
  "description": "SHA-256 (lower-case hex) of the UTF-8 bytes of the RFC 8785 canonical JSON of the content form below. It identifies what was collected: it ignores the sync id, the timestamps, the collector, the catalogue block and anything else outside scope, inventory and assessment_type. 'body' is the request body of POST /syncs; only the fields used here need to be present.",
  "content_form": {
    "assessment_type": "the requested depth as sent",
    "scope": "provider plus the provider block as in the request, with these normalisations: AWS regions sorted and de-duplicated; Azure ids and resource group lower-cased, a null resource group left out; the Terraform lineage lower-cased. Unknown fields are left out.",
    "inventory.resources": "{count, location, type_id} only (type_code is a label and is left out). Items with the same type_id and location are merged by summing counts. Sorted by type_id, then location.",
    "inventory.costs": "{amount, currency, final, month}. amount is normalised as a decimal (no trailing zeros, no exponent, '0' for zero), currency is upper-cased, final defaults to false. Sorted by month, then currency. Omitted costs equal an empty list.",
    "inventory.egress": "{collected, items, names, truncated}. A missing egress block equals {collected: false, items: [], names: 'plain', truncated: false}. Items are {flags, name, notes, size_bytes, tiers, type_id}, with flags and notes sorted, tiers {is_archive, size_bytes, tier} sorted by tier, and the items sorted by type_id, then name."
  },
  "serialisation": [
    "Object keys sorted, no whitespace, strings in UTF-8 without escaping beyond RFC 8785 (non-ASCII characters are written as they are).",
    "Numbers are integers in the I-JSON safe range (at most 9007199254740991 in absolute value). Floats are not allowed."
  ],
